    "updated_at": "2017-02-09T15:03:56Z",
    "body": "I assume the test changes you're requesting are wpt tests?  The problem is that to my knowledge there is no inter-operable way of triggering an encoder error.  A condition that can cause an encoder error is if a memory allocation fails during encoding, but how do you create that condition in a cross-browser test?\r\n\r\nIn Chrome we intend to write a test that simply serializes a webp file that exceeds the maximum dimension allowed by the format (> 16383 in any dimension). But other browsers do not support this format, or in the case of Firefox, it uses an outdated version of the encoder that does not have that limit.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
