    "created_at": "2017-02-15T19:12:08Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-02-15T19:12:08Z",
    "body": "convertToBlob does not throw an exception: it rejects the promise with an exception object.  This is very different. Rejecting a promise with an exception is the normal way for promise-based APIs for signaling an error.\r\nOn the other hand, toBlob is callback based.  Because the error would happen asynchronously (not during script execution), throwing an exception is not possible even if we wanted to.  The only way to communicate the error back to the script is via the callback. ",
